#33001
"Cairn Mountain Road"
"The trail reaches the top of a huge bluff, the bare rock face drops away to

the west down a five hundred foot cliff.  To the east looms the rest of Cairn

mountain which disappears up into the misty clouds.  Snow and ice cover the

trail and it is only the presence of a number of marker stones which stop you

from wandering into a crevasse.

"
