#33002
"Cairn Mountain Road - Atop the Crest"
"To the north the trail starts down the side of the mountain, the track has

been cut out of the rock in the more dangerous places but it will still take

much care.  To the south the trail has levelled off and follows a reasonably

flat path through the ice and snow.  Following the mountain, just this side of

the crest, yet another pathway winds among the boulders, leading west.

"
