#33008
"Cairn Mountains -- Cliff's Edge"
"The trail across the plateau comes dangerously close to the cliff's edge, with

little but thin air between the path and certain death below.  Much of the

dry, loose snow crystals have been blown away here, where nothing protects it

from the blowing wind.  The ledge turns sharply, following the cliff wall

northward and to the west.  The row of pines begins to thin out as it becomes

more exposed to the weather.

"
