the smaller ones seen down the mountainside.  Here upon the jutting stone,

there is little protection from buffeting winds or blowing snow, and underfoot

the ground is slick with a paper-thin layer of ice.  You can climb through the

hole to the east or leave the projection for the shelter of the ledge below.

