#33086
"Crevice"
"The rough grey limestone is close on both sides here, leaving barely enough

room to lead a horse through.  The stony ground is covered in chunks of shale

and small bits of gravel, which are slightly moist due to periodic drips from

the ceiling.  Steadily widening to the north, the crevice leads into a small,

dry cave nestled in the dark limestone.  A rough, rocky slope cuts steeply

downwards into the mist to the south, but looks like it would be a fairly easy

climb.

"
"[Nereus] what goes here :)

