#33087
"Cave in the Limestone"
"Smooth limestone walls encircle this small, conical cave in all directions

except for south, where a small crevice leads out.  The walls seem to have

been smoothed over by years of running water, yet for some reason are

perfectly dry at the moment.  Any ceiling there might be is hidden in the

darkness overhead; the lack of a ceiling makes this cave seem much larger than

it actually is.  The floor is surprisingly smooth and dry, free of all debris

except for a few chunks of loose shale.

"
"[Kotoktok] added room

